  Vulnerability: The strongest objection is that retrofitting AI accountability onto existing tort and corporate liability frameworks may systematically underperform: liability regimes are backward-looking and compensatory, whereas the most catastrophic AI risks are diffuse, probabilistic, and may materialize long after deployment decisions are made, meaning that even well-designed strict liability rules cannot deter harms whose causal chains are too attenuated or whose damages exceed any developer's solvency.
